---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import AssistantSetup from "../components/AssistantSetup.astro";
import MemoDemo from "../components/MemoDemo.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Milton keeps the writing you approved, word for word"
  description="Your AI has a case of the Mondays in every new chat. Milton keeps what you wrote, from emails to speeches, so the next draft sounds like you."
>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="headline">
    <div>
      <h1 id="headline">
        Milton keeps the writing you approved, word for word.
      </h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Your AI has a case of the Mondays in every new chat. Milton keeps what
        you wrote, from emails to speeches, so the next draft sounds like you.
        It’s a filing cabinet. We’re proud.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-aside">
        Everyone else is building superintelligence. We’re asking it to stop
        using em dashes.
      </p>
      <div class="actions action-row">
        <a class="button" href="https://app.meetmilton.com/login">
          Try Milton free <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <AssistantSetup />
      </div>
    </div>
    <MemoDemo />
  </section>
  <div class="assistant-strip">
    <span class="assistant-label">Works with:</span>
    <nav aria-label="AI setup guides">
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="/setup#claude">Claude</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/setup#chatgpt">ChatGPT</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/setup#claude-code">Claude Code</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/setup#codex">Codex</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/setup#cursor">Cursor</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/setup">and more</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </div>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="scope-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">## Less rewriting</p>
    <h2 id="scope-heading">
      Your AI should write like you before it writes for you.
    </h2>
    <p class="section-lead">
      Save something you actually wrote, and every AI you connect writes the
      next one like you. Yeah, that’d be great.
    </p>
    <div class="use-cases">
      <article class="use-case">
        <h3>The voice you carry.</h3>
        <p>
          Samples you approved: the follow-up you actually sent, the connection
          note that worked. Rules for what a sample cannot show: greetings,
          sign-offs, length, and the phrases you never use.
        </p>
        <p class="sample-rule">
          “Use at most one exclamation point, in the opening line.”
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="use-case">
        <h3>Every kind of writing.</h3>
        <p>
          Emails, messages, posts, docs, and the toast you give once a year.
          Each gets its own samples and rules.
        </p>
        <p class="sample-rule">
          “Docs: say ‘I recommend,’ not ‘it is recommended.’”
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">## Less repeating. Less paperwork.</p>
    <h2 id="how-heading">Tell it once. Keep it on file.</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Connect your AI.</h3>
        <p>
          Add Milton through your AI’s MCP or connector settings and sign in to
          your Milton account.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/setup">Find your setup instructions →</a>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Approve a draft. Keep it.</h3>
        <p>
          When a draft is right, say so. Your AI shows you the exact text and
          asks before saving it as a sample. Correct the same thing twice and it
          proposes a rule for your yes. Starting from scratch? Paste one email
          you sent, then pick between short examples, one question at a time.
          One approved email is enough to start.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Bring it to the next chat.</h3>
        <p>
          Ask “did you get that memo?” to load your cover sheet and the report
          that fits: email, chat, post, document, or speech. Tell your AI what
          to add, correct, or remove as your writing changes.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="reading-note small-note">
      <strong class="memo-limit">
        We distribute the memo. We cannot make everyone read it.
      </strong>
      Ask your AI to read your Milton cover sheet when you start work. It isn’t
      automatically included in every chat, and following it is still up to the
      AI.
    </p>
    <div class="where-to-start" id="where-to-start">
      <p class="eyebrow">## Onboarding</p>
      <h3>Not sure where to start?</h3>
      <p>
        Say “set up Milton” to your AI and answer a few questions. That’s the
        onboarding. No call, no specialist, no calendar link. We looked into
        offering one and decided it could have been an email. Email{" "}
        <a href="mailto:lumbergh@meetmilton.com">lumbergh@meetmilton.com</a> and
        nobody will read it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section
    class="section control-section"
    id="your-preferences"
    aria-labelledby="control-heading"
  >
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">## You stay in control</p>
      <h2 id="control-heading">We won’t take your stapler.</h2>
      <p class="portability-copy">
        Check it yourself. The source is public, and you can run Milton
        yourself. Download TPS.md to see what your AI reads. Disconnect an AI
        and Milton refuses it at once.
      </p>
      <p class="portability-aside">
        We’d prefer you keep paying us, but apparently that’s not a retention
        strategy.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/zoneofdanger/milton">Read the source ↗</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="employee-testimonial" id="employee-testimonial">
      <p class="eyebrow">## Fictional employee testimonial</p>
      <blockquote>
        “Milton lets me say ‘Did you get that memo?’ to software. I have never
        felt more qualified for management.”
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Michael Bolton</strong>
        <span>Senior Founding AI Forward Deployed Product Engineer</span>
      </figcaption>
      <p class="carousel-count">
        <span class="carousel-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>1 of 1
      </p>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <section
    class="section pricing"
    id="pricing"
    aria-labelledby="pricing-heading"
  >
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">## One plan. We resisted making three columns.</p>
      <h2 id="pricing-heading">Less repeating yourself.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        One plan for your writing voice, whether you use one AI or several.
      </p>
      <p class="reading-note small-note">
        Early access is free while we prepare paid subscriptions. No card is
        required, and signing up today won’t charge you.
      </p>
      <p class="reading-note small-note">
        After your free trial, subscribe to keep AI access. You can still view
        and download your report without a subscription.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="sheet price-card">
      <div class="sheet-bar">
        <span>Planned launch pricing</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sheet-content">
        <p class="price">
          <strong>$5.01</strong> <span>USD / month</span>
        </p>
        <p>Five dollars for Milton. One cent for accounting.</p>
        <p>30 days free. No credit card required.</p>
        <ul class="badges">
          <li>Not AI-powered. Your AI is.</li>
          <li>Enterprise-grade asking nicely.</li>
          <li>Synergy, pending approval.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small-note badge-issuer">
          A founder who has mistaken this for a company.
        </p>
        <a class="button" href="https://app.meetmilton.com/login">
          Try free early access <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">## A few things to know</p>
    <h2 id="faq-heading">Before you connect.</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>What does Milton keep, and what does it never touch?</summary>
      <p>
        Only what you approve: samples of your writing, kept word for word, and
        the rules you ask for, stored as your AI sends them. Milton never
        rewrites a rule or a sample. It never reads your inbox, your files, or
        your conversations.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is it useful if I only use Claude?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes. Keep one voice across conversations with the same AI, with samples
        it can imitate instead of adjectives it has to interpret. Connecting
        another AI later is optional.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How is this different from memory tools?</summary>
      <p>
        Memory tools remember your birthday. Milton remembers you’ve never once
        written “I hope this finds you well.” Milton stores how you write:
        writing you approved, quoted exactly, and the rules you asked for, in a
        form every AI can read. Keep facts, documents, and project history in
        the tools you already use. Milton is the voice layer beside whatever
        remembers your work.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does Milton build a profile of my voice?</summary>
      <p>
        No. Your AI reads your samples exactly as you approved them, then your
        rules. Nothing summarizes or paraphrases them, so there is no profile to
        drift away from what you wrote.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why not use custom instructions or AGENTS.md?</summary>
      <p>
        Those can work well. Milton gives you one place to keep your voice
        without copying changes between AIs or project files. Keep
        project-specific setup in those files, and ask your AI to read Milton
        for how you write.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Which AIs can I connect?</summary>
      <p>
        Milton uses MCP. Your AI needs support for a remote MCP server, sign-in,
        and both reading and saving through tools. Availability depends on your
        AI, plan, and workspace settings.{" "}
        <a href="/setup">Check the setup guide before signing up.</a>
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What can an AI do with Milton?</summary>
      <p>
        Four things: read your cover sheet, read a report, list your reports,
        and save what you approve. It can’t send anything, read any other
        account, or browse on your behalf.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What’s the cover sheet? What’s a report?</summary>
      <p>
        The cover sheet holds the rules true of all your writing and an index of
        five reports: email, chat, post, document, and speech. Each report holds
        the samples you approved for that kind of writing, then its rules. Your
        AI handles the filing; you don’t manage a memo list. The names are an
        Office Space reference. The paperwork is less demanding.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What do my connected AIs share?</summary>
      <p>
        Each can read your cover sheet and reports, samples included, exactly as
        you approved them. Keep private project context in its own tools. Milton
        doesn’t import another service’s memory or your conversation history.
      </p>
      <p>
        Samples are saved only when you say yes, and stored as written, names
        included. Rules are stored exactly as your AI sends them; Milton never
        rewrites a rule or a sample.{" "}
        <a href="/privacy">Read the privacy policy.</a>
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will my AI always write like me?</summary>
      <p>
        Not always. Milton keeps the samples and rules available. Ask your AI to
        read them when you start work; the AI still decides how closely to
        follow them.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will I be charged after signing up?</summary>
      <p>
        No. Early access is currently free and we don’t collect payment details.
        The planned paid offer is $5.01 USD/month after a 30-day free trial. No
        credit card is required to try it, and you won’t be charged unless you
        subscribe.
      </p>
      <p>
        After an unsubscribed trial ends at paid launch, AI reads and saves will
        pause. Your cover sheet and reports will remain available on the website
        to view and download.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why the extra penny?</summary>
      <p>We’ve been assured the accounting software is working as intended.</p>
    </details>
    <details id="why-milton">
      <summary>Why does this exist?</summary>
      <p>
        Peter wanted his AIs to write like him. Somehow he ended up building
        them a filing department.
      </p>
      <p class="eyebrow">## An imaginary productivity review</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Reviewer:</strong> Walk us through a typical session.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Me:</strong> First I explain how I like to work. Then I remind
        it. Then it apologizes. Then I explain that I don’t need the apology.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Reviewer:</strong> How much actual work gets done?
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Me:</strong> About fifteen minutes.
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>
  <section class="closing">
    <p class="eyebrow">## Did you get that memo?</p>
    <h2>Let’s put that in a memo.</h2>
    <p>
      We did not build superintelligence. We built a drawer. Cover sheets
      optional.
    </p>
    <a class="button" href="https://app.meetmilton.com/login">
      Try Milton free <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  :where(h1, h2:not(.sheet-heading), h3, p, figure) {
    margin: 0;
  }
  /* No paragraph ends on a lone word. Scoped to this page, so the demo's
     typed lines keep plain wrapping. */
  p,
  blockquote {
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: var(--space-20);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-hero);
    line-height: 1.18;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .intro {
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    max-width: 36em;
  }
  .hero-aside {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .actions {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .assistant-strip {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .assistant-label {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: var(--touch-target);
  }
  .assistant-strip ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0 var(--space-2);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .assistant-strip li {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
  }
  /* Even separators between names; the dot is decoration, not read aloud. */
  .assistant-strip li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: "·";
    content: "·" / "";
    margin-left: var(--space-2);
  }
  .assistant-strip a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: var(--touch-target);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .section {
    padding-block: var(--space-20);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .section h2 {
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    font-size: var(--text-section);
    margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
  }
  .section h2 span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .section-lead {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
  }
  .use-cases {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }
  .use-case {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .use-cases {
      row-gap: 0;
    }
    .use-case {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-rows: subgrid;
      grid-row: span 3;
    }
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-title);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .use-case p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .use-case .sample-rule {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding-top: var(--space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
  }
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-8);
    padding: 0;
    margin: var(--space-8) 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
  }
  .steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
  }
  .steps li::before {
    content: "0" counter(step);
    font: var(--text-caption) / var(--leading-label) var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .steps h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .steps p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .pricing {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }
  .steps p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .pricing {
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-16);
  }
  .price {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .price strong {
    font: var(--font-display-weight) var(--text-hero) / var(--leading-heading)
      var(--font-display);
  }
  .price span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }
  /* Compliance-style chips: statements, not controls. Rounded, hairline and
     mono so they cannot pass for the square, filled buttons. */
  .badges {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .badges li {
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-control);
    background: var(--ground);
    color: var(--ink);
    font: var(--text-caption) / var(--leading-label) var(--font-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }
  .price-card .badge-issuer {
    margin-block: var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
  }

  .reading-note {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }
  .where-to-start {
    max-width: 75ch;
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }
  .where-to-start h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .where-to-start p:not(.eyebrow) {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .control-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-16);
  }
  .portability-copy {
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
  }
  .portability-aside {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-block: var(--space-5);
  }
  .faq details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
  }
  .faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style-position: outside;
    margin-inline-start: var(--space-5);
    min-height: var(--touch-target);
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .faq details p {
    max-width: 75ch;
    margin-block: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .closing {
    text-align: center;
    padding-block: var(--space-20);
  }
  .closing h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-section);
    margin-block: var(--space-4);
  }
  .closing p:not(.eyebrow) {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  @media (min-width: 861px) and (max-width: 1100px) {
    .hero {
      gap: var(--space-8);
      padding-block: var(--space-12);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    h1 {
      max-width: 660px;
    }
    .intro {
      max-width: 45ch;
    }

    .control-section {
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-10);
      padding-block: var(--space-12);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .control-section {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-10);
    }
    .assistant-strip {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }
    .assistant-label {
      min-height: auto;
    }
    .section,
    .closing {
      padding-block: var(--space-12);
    }
    .use-cases,
    .steps,
    .pricing {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-6);
    }
    .hero {
      padding-block: var(--space-10);
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }
    .intro {
      font-size: var(--text-body);
      margin-top: var(--space-5);
    }
    .actions .button {
      padding-inline: var(--space-5);
    }
    .section-lead {
      font-size: var(--text-body);
    }
    .use-case {
      padding: var(--space-6);
    }
    .badges {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
  }
  .memo-limit {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--ink);
    font: var(--font-display-weight) var(--text-title) / var(--leading-heading)
      var(--font-display);
  }
  .employee-testimonial {
    margin: 0;
    align-self: center;
  }
  .employee-testimonial blockquote {
    max-width: 40ch;
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
    font: var(--font-display-weight) var(--text-section) /
      var(--leading-heading) var(--font-display);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .employee-testimonial figcaption {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }
  .employee-testimonial figcaption span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  /* Where a carousel puts its dots: one testimonial, one dot. Nothing to click. */
  .carousel-count {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--muted);
    font: var(--text-caption) / var(--leading-label) var(--font-mono);
  }
  .carousel-dot {
    flex: none;
    width: var(--space-2);
    height: var(--space-2);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
